      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Percutaneous transluminal coronary angioplasty (PTCA) of shepherd's crook right coronary arteries presents a difficult technical challenge. Presented here are two cases demonstrating the use of an internal mammary guiding catheter for PTCA of shepherd's crook right coronary arteries. The advantages of this guiding catheter, a short tip with an acute distal angle, are emphasized."},
